  "body": "Follow-up to #131 / PR #162. That PR ships the Tormach PathPilot post and one machine, the **770MX** (`assets/machines/tormach-770mx.mch`, inch). Tormach's other current and recent mills have no machine file yet:\n\n- 1500MX\n- 1100MX\n- 1100 (non-MX; the #131 thread mentions testing on one)\n- 770 and 770M (non-MX)\n- PCNC 440\n\n### What each needs\nOne `.mch` per machine (inch, `\"kind\": \"mill\"`), added to `posting::MACHINES` and to `machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration`, with:\n- X/Y/Z travel;\n- spindle min/max rpm, power, and taper;\n- belt ranges;\n- X/Y and Z maximum feed;\n- ATC capacity, if the machine has one;\n- coolant codes.\n\n**Source:** each machine's own Tormach operator's manual (§ \"Machine Specifications\"), which is public Tormach documentation and allowed under the Clean-Room Protocol. The contributor has the manuals and can share them. The 770MX one (UM10587) and the 1100MX one (UM10586) are already in hand.\n\n### Things that may differ from the 770MX and touch the post\n- **Belt ranges.** The post's belt-range comment hard-codes the 770 family's ranges (low 175–3250, high 525–10000 rpm). Other models have other ranges, so those numbers should come from the machine file, which would need a small `.mch` field.\n- **Rigid tapping.** The non-MX machines (R8 spindle) may not rigid-tap. The post writes `G84` on every Tormach machine today, so a machine without rigid tapping should refuse a tap by name, which needs a capability flag in the `.mch`.\n- **The MicroArc 4th axis** stays in #131's scope and isn't part of this issue.\n\nSuggested labels (the filer can't set labels): `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:post`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
